						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#79">Guild Charter</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							The Lords of Rage ranking system is as follows:<br />
Guild Leader, Asst. Guild Leader, Senior Officer, Officer, Member, Initiate.<br />
<br />
The Guild Board will consist of the Guild Leader, the Asst. Guild Leader, Sr. Officers and Officers.<br />
<br />
The Asst. Guild Leader is appointed by the Guild Leader. The Asst. Guild Leader for all intents and purposes has the same authority as the Guild Leader. In my absence the Asst. word is my own.<br />
   <br />
Senior Officers should be nominated out of the officer pool and will require a 2/3-majority vote of the membership.<br />
<br />
Officers are nominated out of the member pool and will require a majority vote of the Guild Membership.<br />
   <br />
Members are Full members of the Guild. For voting purposes a member is considered to have a vote if the votes comes from their PRIMARY Character that is in the guild. This also applies when determining the number of officers in the guild at any particular time. We do not need an officer because someone has 5 characters in the guild. <br />
   <br />
Initiates are not members of the Guild but are potential new members, awaiting approval by the Guild.<br />
<br />
The Guild Leader Asst. Guild Leader and Officers will make decisions based on the good of the guild. Should the change and/or requirements of the guild change in any way that will effect more than half of the members, a full vote will be required by all persons in the guild. The Guild Leader holds two votes and the privilege of a veto, The Asst. Leader and all Officers one each. <br />
<br />
There will be 1 Guild Leader<br />
There will be 1 Asst. Guild Leader<br />
There will be 3 Senior Officers<br />
There will be any number of officers with an attempt to maintain a ratio of 1 Officer per 5 members to start.<br />
<br />
Three committees are to be formed each committee will be led by a Sr. Officer. Each committee will initially be formed of 3 people. 1 Sr.Officer to lead that committee and any 2 members that a) Volunteer or b) are assigned because there are no volunteers. <br />
<br />
The Event Committee is responsible for planning all Guild Events. Any member of the guild can submit ideas for events to the Event Committee. An Event can be anything from a full guild raid to simple assistance in helping a member obtain a needed quest item.  These things SHOULD be planned. If an event is NOT planned through the Event Committee and someone wants to organize a spur of the moment event that is fine, but the Guild membership will NOT be obligated to assist for NON PLANNED EVENTS. All members are encouraged to participate in any and all guild events; Active participation will certainly look more favorable to you when you are suggesting new members, as you are more likely to recruit someone who is comparable to yourself. Final decision on events lie within the Events Committee. Members are rarely required to attend events, but the guild as a whole benefits, the more people partake. <br />
<br />
The Recruitment Committee is responsible for active recruitment of new members to the Guild. Also, they are responsible for evaluating new initiates suggested by the membership at large. The Recruitment Committee’s final recommendation will be heavily taken into account when deciding on membership status for Initiates and in most cases will be final. It is suggested that at least 2 members of the committee observe the Initiate on different occasions. This may not always be possible and they will rely heavily on the opinions of the general membership that has grouped/witnessed actions good or bad by the initiate. <br />
<br />
The Complaint Committee is responsible for taking and handling member complaints. This is going to be a difficult one to enforce, as there will be times that there is no one from this committee available. It is the Complaint Committee’s responsibility to take member complaints and try to resolve those complaints in the best interest of the guild. Any decision by the complaint committee that involves the termination of membership to an individual from the guild will be reviewed by all Officers, Senior Officer, Asst Leader and <br />
Guild Leader for review and vote. A majority vote of the Guild Board is required to terminate a member’s membership in the guild. In the absence of a complaint committee member complaints can be made to any officer or above who happens to be online. Complaints shout be just that. Complaints not whining, not bellyaching not a knee jerk reaction to something that just pissed you off. I do not wish to see any board member inundated with the Bullshit that the previous leadership went through. We are all here to have fun and that’s what it should be. If a person is a member of LoR it is for a good reason. It is because they are worthy of the title. As such that respect should be shown to everyone in the guild from the leader down to the newest member. Disrespect will not be tolerated and will be dealt with swiftly and harshly. Bear in mind that when a complaint is made it is taking time out of someone else’s game enjoyment. Ask yourself. Is this really important enough that I would want my game interrupted for it if I was the one receiving the complaint? <br />
<br />
Looting: I don’t have a lot to say about this except that as in any group loot rules should be established beforehand. Basic guidelines that should be followed include item drops that are useable within the group should be awarded to the people who can use them before they are awarded to people who are going to sell them. If a group has been camping a spot for some time looking for a particular item and members have to leave and new ones take there place preference should go to the ones who have been there the longest. Simply just try to be fair..
						</td>
